WEBVTT

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:04.980
Kuma!

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.180
Kumagoro!

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.660
Kumagoro, where are you?

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.410
We're going to the doctor's!

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.220
Takanashi

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:01.700
<b>Episode 9:   My Maid And The Day We Met</b>

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.700
Kumagoro...

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.090
Where are you hiding?

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.560
Milady, is there an issue?

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.380
Nothing really.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.120
You're so wonderfully modest.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.000
You can ask me for anything 
you need, you know?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.040
I don't think there exists someone in 
this world who would be modest with you.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.770
You guys.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.820
Do you know where Kumagoro is?

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.940
Really?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.560
<b>Pressure</b>

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.890
He jumped off the patio?

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.060
This isn't good...

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.320
We have to go find him!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.460
I need to inform the police and post 
on the lost pet forums online...

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.940
O-Oh, yeah! I need to make fliers!

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.000
Milady, please calm down.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.280
I can't remain calm!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.120
Huh?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.330
In an situation where every moment matters,

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.340
do you plan on doing everything on your own?

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:57.560
I see...

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.720
Now, ask me for help!

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.260
I'm gonna call Washiwashi.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.920
Huh?

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:03.340
Hello?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.580
Sure, no problem.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.720
Leave the fliers to me.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:10.310
My mother's into those 
detective shows as of late.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.600
I think she'd really want to help.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:15.510
I'll head to the police.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.430
You look for Kumagoro-sama.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.220
We'll meet up later.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.610
Watch out for any cars.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:24.360
Thanks...

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.610
<b>Love</b>

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.520
Yes.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:32.330
Let's go get married right 
after we find Kumagoro-sama.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.380
Or you could go get cremated 
alive, instead. Alone.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.250
Kumagoro!

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.260
Kumagoro!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.680
Kuma!

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.640
<i>This isn't going to work.</i>

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.750
<i>Ferrets like hiding in small 
places and nooks and crannies.</i>

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.970
<i>They also dig holes in the ground.</i>

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:55.220
<i>I won't find him just by 
looking in random places.</i>

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.980
<i>But without Kumagoro...</i>

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.340
Mommy...

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.500
Don't leave me alone, Mommy.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.580
Misha, I'm going to come in.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.190
Misha.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.910
T-Tada.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:30.720
Huh?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.820
Open it up, Misha.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.500
He'll be part of our family from now on.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.700
You think you can take care of him?

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.460
Y-Yeah!

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.200
Kumagoro...

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.940
Milady!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.510
Did you find him?

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:56.760
No.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.420
Not even a hint about where he is.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.730
Maybe I just won't be able to find him.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:06.020
If Kumagoro leaves me, 
I'll be all alone again...

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.320
Do you really think you're alone?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:11.880
Huh?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.930
<b>Looking for a Ferret</b>

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.930
<b>Ferret (Male)
If you find him, please call the number below.</b>

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:19.350
I'm not going to lie and say we're 
definitely going to find him.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.190
<b>Neighborhood Bulletin Board</b>

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.120
But if you give up,

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.860
you're going to regret it in the future.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.610
Let's do our best to find him.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.620
I-I'm not going to give up!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.450
I just got a little disheartened.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.490
That's the spirit.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.370
Besides, you have me, don't you?

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.060
Kuma!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.130
No!

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:47.300
A police dog would be able to sniff him out.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.260
We don't have enough manpower.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.190
I didn't want to depend on her,

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.010
but I guess I don't have a choice.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.640
It's time for food.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.520
You wait until I say it's okay.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.720
<i>You didn't wait at all!</i>

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:11.120
<i>You're looking down on me.</i>

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.920
Oh, it's a German Shepherd!

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:13.660
Hmm?

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.180
Isn't that Meteor?

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.850
It looks like him, but it isn't.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.040
This is Meteor's older brother, Racing Cloud.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.290
I see. They look the same.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.990
I took him in when he 
retired as a police dog.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:31.970
Oh, I see.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.160
When a military working dog retires,

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.870
he just lives the rest of his 
life on the base, after all.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.570
Now we have a police dog!

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.820
Find Kumagoro for me.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.070
Wow! That's a former police dog, for you!

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.600
What?!

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.890
Well, I'm sure this place does smell of him.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.450
Not here!

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:59.010
Find a place other than here 
that has the same smell!

00:07:59.010 --> 00:07:59.940
Understand?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.780
Seems like he wants to play.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.660
Racing Cloud.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:10.840
Find him.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:18.710
He listens to her immediately when he just 
met Kamoi, but he doesn't listen to me!

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:19.820
Let's go.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.350
Th-This is the place?

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.980
It's Takanashi and the Master.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.820
What are you doing?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:31.820
Morikawa-san!

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:32.860
Why are you here?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.710
Why? This is my house.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.500
Huh?

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.360
So you kidnapped him, then?!

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.480
What are you talking about?

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.380
Well...

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.540
So you're searching for your 
ferret that ran away.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.600
But he's not here.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.880
But Racing Cloud is saying that his 
smell is coming from your house.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.200
If you don't trust me that much, 
then go ahead and take a look.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.760
In exchange...

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.420
If you can't find him,

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.880
then you have to admit 
that I'm cuter than you!

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.560
That's a weird condition.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.770
No way he's here, though.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:10.660
There he is!

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:11.800
Kumagoro!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.370
A good lolita!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.250
Kamoi?!

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.660
<b>Love</b>

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:21.990
That's terrible.

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:25.020
Anyway, Yuina! Why do you have that?!

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.040
It's a muffler!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:26.830
It's cool!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.000
The latest fashion!

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.330
You can't have that.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:31.250
He's Takanashi's pet.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.640
Give him back!

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.590
Kumagoro isn't a muffler!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.800
No, I picked him up!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.650
He's my muffler!

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.890
No, Kumagoro is my pet!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.390
He's my family!

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:52.820
Look, there's a cute little 
girl right here in the street.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.320
I picked you up, so now
I guess that makes you mine.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.200
I'm going to take you back to my house,

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.470
and make you into my doll.

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.370
Lolicon punishment!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.220
My body reacted instinctively.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.840
Let me down!

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:16.710
Then will you give Kumagoro-sama back?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:18.860
I will...

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.690
Here.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:28.240
Kumagoro!

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.450
Takanashi, I'm sorry.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.700
My sister caused you all this trouble.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.880
Morikawa-san...

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.720
Now you apologize, too!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.150
You can't take other people's stuff!

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:40.910
I'm sorry.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:41.880
It's okay.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.240
You're still a kid, anyway.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.410
You, too.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.550
In any event, all's well that ends well.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:48.190
Yeah!

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.920
I need to call Washiwashi.

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:51.540
Kumagoro!

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:54.320
Now let's go to the doctor's.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Uzamaid!</b>

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.930
<b>Uzamaid!</b>

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.970
<i>I-It's cold.</i>

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.680
<i>I can't get up...</i>

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.940
<i>I don't want to get out of bed.</i>

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.790
Good morning!

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.080
<i>Darn it... I wasted time 
not getting out of bed,</i>

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.750
<i>and now she got here before I got up!</i>

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.700
<i>I normally head down before 
she makes it up here.</i>

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.150
Milady, excuse me.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:32.780
Huh?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.680
It snowed!

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.490
There's a lot of it out there.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.370
Yes, indeed.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.140
Does that mean school's out today?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.000
Huh?

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.020
You know, the traffic infrastructure 
of the Kanto area in Japan

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.600
doesn't handle snow very well.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.300
I'm sure school's out.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.560
You walk to school, don't you?

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.730
Wake up!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.400
Children should be outside!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.540
My parents never treated me like this!

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.120
I don't want to go...

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:08.280
The snow's going to get in 
through the top of my boots,

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.160
and then get the insides all wet...

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:14.250
Then my feet are going to get all 
cold from the snow that melts.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:15.880
Milady...

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:19.800
You used to run around outside in the snow.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:24.260
Well, my mom liked the snow, so I was 
just kind of making my mom happy.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:25.390
<i>She's an adult.</i>

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.510
I don't like the snow.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.840
Then I'll carry you on my 
back all the way to school!

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.770
If you want, I can lift you up off your feet 
like a princess and carry you that way!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.650
Talk to you later!

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.520
No!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.530
Huh?

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.270
There's no snow.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.860
Oh, Midorin!

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:48.410
Oh, good morning.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.520
You're the one who shoveled all the snow?

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.240
Yeah.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.560
I would shovel, and then more 
snow would just pile up.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:59.120
Humans pale in comparison 
to the force that is nature.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.880
What a waste of time.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.880
But it started snowing in 
the middle of the night.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.610
And I've been up all night, of course!

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:07.610
Midorin, try not to die too early.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:10.030
I couldn't shovel all the way to your school,

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.460
but some of the other residents 
have cleared their snow.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.890
I'm sure you can get quite 
far without getting wet.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.310
Thank you!

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.270
See you later!

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.990
Goodbye!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:25.480
First Lieutenant,

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.280
<b>Older Lady Store</b>

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.280
please use this tissue.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.570
Thanks for your hard work.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.270
Y-You're giving these to me?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:36.910
I'll treasure them forever!

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.210
Use them and throw them away.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.240
Misha-chan, good morning.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.050
Good morning!

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.680
The second semester is going to end today.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:52.810
Washiwashi.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:53.460
Hmm?

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.180
Did you get fatter?

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.000
Y-You can tell?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.060
I guess.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:01.220
You know in the winter,

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.820
there's a bunch of limited 
time chocolate candies, right?

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:08.710
If I don't pay attention, my little 
brothers will eat all of them.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:09.570
Hey!

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.780
You guys are eating them 
without telling me again!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.080
<b>Survival of the Fittest</b>

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.080
That's what it's like to have siblings, huh?

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:22.370
Also, it's cold, so you know, you 
don't want to move around much.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:23.520
Oh, I understand that.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.580
I don't want to get all wet from the snow.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:25.960
Huh?

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:28.590
You look good out in the snow, though.

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.170
Huh?

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.820
It reminds me of my mother, who died.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.660
U-Uh...

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.060
Want to run?

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.520
It'll warm us up.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.090
Yeah.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:48.070
It'll help me lose weight.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:48.490
Yeah.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:49.740
Let's go.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:50.820
Start!

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.870
Yui-chan, aren't you cold dressed like that?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.400
I'm not going to dress up unfashionably by 
adding all these layers just because it's cold.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.710
That's not happening for 
someone as hip as me.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.420
I'll fend off the cold with pure will.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.700
I'm tired.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.530
I don't usually exercise.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:17.850
I'm glad all we have to do is have our 
semester ending ceremony and clean today.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:21.070
Huh? Did Takanashi-san get a new coat?

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.810
You're right. I guess because it's so cold.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:27.020
I guess if a truly cute little girl dresses 
up in layers and gets all puffed up,

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:28.070
she's still cute!

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.820
Takanashi!

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:31.700
Huh?

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.450
Let's fight!

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.200
Huh? Why?

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:40.960
She challenged her, but really 
hadn't thought of any challenge.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.630
I guess she just lives in the moment?

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.560
Uh... I...

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:52.340
We're going to have a snowball 
fight since it just snowed!

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.520
Huh?

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:57.170
That's like saying "because it's sunny out."

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:00.810
And she's just picking 
something she's good at.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.570
There's no real reason for me to accept.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:07.680
I'm good at snowball fights, so 
you and Washizaki can team up.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.750
I'll give you a handicap.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.950
Why are you acting like I'm going to do this?

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.470
Misha-chan, let's do this challenge.

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:16.190
Huh?

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:16.860
What?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:22.710
Wants to lose weight

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.710
Well, I guess it's fine.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.330
Then it's decided.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.380
We're doing it in the 
schoolyard after school!

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:31.090
Washiwashi, you're acting all different.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.720
The time limit is ten minutes.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:40.470
The person team that lands the 
most hit with snowballs wins.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.100
Who's going to count?

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.510
Right here!

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:45.980
My grandfather is a birdwatcher!

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.360
And why would that matter 
to you, his granddaughter...

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.510
Okay, going to start!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.610
Ready...

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.150
Go!

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.630
Take this!

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:56.480
It's fast!

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.840
In any event, we should put 
some distance between us.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:00.660
Yeah!

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:03.840
Misha-chan!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.580
Hey!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:06.780
Take this!

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:10.750
Take this!

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:14.360
You suck! You suck! You suck!

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.780
What should we do?

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.750
You should split up your roles.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:18.470
Huh?

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:19.800
What?

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:22.230
I'm a snowman, passing by.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:24.230
Snowmen can't pass by anything!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.880
Washizaki-sama has trouble 
controlling her throws,

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.430
so she can make the snowballs.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:34.030
And then you distract 
Morikawa-sama and attack her!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.650
I-I see.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:39.030
What are you talking about over there?!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.060
<i>Wait, if I leave the snowball 
making to Washiwashi,</i>

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.370
<i>then I can focus on running, and 
we might just win this thing!</i>

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:49.600
Washiwashi!

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.000
Misha-chan!

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.100
Washiwashi, I want you to move 
around and make lots of snowballs.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.970
I'll do the attacking.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.470
Got it!

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.930
Morikawa-san, over here!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.640
You've got guts!

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:05.680
Take this!

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:08.300
Hey!

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.060
Take that!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:13.610
<i>Now Morikawa-san is only attacking me!</i>

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:18.740
Stop moving around so much!

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.490
Misha-chan, use the snowballs over there!

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:22.740
Okay!

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.120
Take this!

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:26.370
What?!

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.120
Yeah, we got her!

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:29.810
I see...

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.880
So you split up, and only one of 
you is making the snowballs.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.000
In that case...

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.560
I'm not going to let you do that!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.580
I'm going to protect you, Washiwashi!

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:40.760
Misha-chan...

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:45.750
Washizaki-sama.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:47.220
What?!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.180
A snowman?

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:51.120
I thought you were over there a second ago...

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.840
Actually, did you just talk?

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:57.390
Take off your gloves, and make 
the snowballs as hard as you can.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:00.720
Huh? Are you Misha-chan's maid?

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:01.460
Hurry!

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.530
Right!

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.210
Milady, throw as many 
snowballs as you possibly can,

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.200
and get Morikawa-sama 
to back away.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:09.000
Got it.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.460
Now I can't get close!

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:14.880
In that case, all I have to 
do is throw from far away.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.090
I can handle this much better than you two 
can with my arm and my throwing control!

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:20.790
Misha-chan!

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.340
I can't get away!

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.680
Darn it! I guess I didn't 
pack it hard enough!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.720
Milady, now!

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:32.740
But at this distance...

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.650
Believe in yourself and Washizaki-sama!

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.150
Misha-chan...

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:40.650
Got it!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.820
Take this!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.560
Ow!

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.830
That was hard!

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.330
I got her...

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:53.780
Because you directly formed 
the snowballs with your hands,

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:55.410
the outer snow melted with from 
the temperature of your body,

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.500
and then when you compacted 
them, they got even harder.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.620
That's how you make super strong 
snowballs that won't break,

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.970
even if you throw them as hard as you can!

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:04.380
I see!

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:06.600
Misha-chan, I'll make even more!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.220
Yeah!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:12.930
I can't make snowballs when I'm running!

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.490
This isn't fair!

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.110
No, you set these terms!

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.980
Take this!

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.740
Hasn't ten minutes passed already?!

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.960
I can't wait to see what I get in 
my New Year's gift mystery bags.

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:27.670
Just get stuff off the Internet.

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:30.520
Ref, ten minutes is up!

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:31.040
Huh?

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.320
Time!

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:34.330
Come on.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:37.050
Now, who won?

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:37.950
Huh?

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:39.910
Sorry.

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:41.740
I stopped watching halfway through.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.360
Darn it!

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.270
I mean everything went by so 
fast, it was hard to tell.

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:48.720
What happened to being the 
granddaughter of a birdwatcher?

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.470
Then let's call it a tie.

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:56.140
I'll let you get off with 
that just for today!

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:59.260
Well, if we counted, you might have lost.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:01.400
That's not true!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.460
Good work, Misha-chan!

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.780
Washiwashi, your hands are all red.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.290
Well, I was directly touching the snow.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.170
Misha-chan!

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:24.360
We were able to fight back because 
you made snowballs for me.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:26.020
Thank your.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:29.360
Misha-chan, do you like it more now?

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:30.180
Huh?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:31.820
The snow.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:33.740
Yeah.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:36.550
I was able to have fun!

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:39.990
So precious... So precious...

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:40.440
Huh?

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.590
So precious... So precious...

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:44.610
Hey!

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:47.570
Why are you here, anyway?!

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:52.610
When I look at snow, I remember 
the first day I met you.

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:56.240
I couldn't let a chance to see a young Russian
 girl playing around in the snow go by!

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:00.920
I was just about to remember this day as 
something fun that happened, and now...

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:05.920
Don't overwrite my fun memory with 
one of some pervert spying on me!
